target/
target-dev/
**/*.rs.bk
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
.vscode/
.target-cleanup/

# Refacto v1.0.0-beta.1: legacy crates parked here for cherry-pick during the
# rewrite. Local-only — never committed.
.old/

# Standardoc runtime artifacts (created by the daemon when dogfooding the
# tool on its own repo). User projects WILL want to commit `.standardoc/pages/`
# and `.standardoc/keys.lock.json` — but this repo has nothing meaningful to
# ship there. Pattern is anchored at root (`/`) so the demo `.standardoc/`
# folders inside `examples/*/` stay tracked.
/.standardoc/
/.standardoc-sessions/
.standarflow
ext/vscode/.standardoc/
sessions-export/
.claude/
.mcp.json

# IDE / editor metadata — left to contributor preference
.idea/

# Web frontend = Standardoc Pro (closed-source, separate distribution).
# The `standardoc-web` crate is feature-gated (`embedded-frontend`):
# OSS builds skip `web/` entirely. Pro builds require it populated from
# the private `standardoc-pro` repo before `cargo build --features ...`.
web/
.sbuild-cache

# Rendered docs — outputs of `scripts/render-docs.sh`. Source of truth lives
# in `docs-src/`. CI re-renders on push to main and force-commits the result
# (`git add -f` over this gitignore) so the GitHub view stays current.
# Contributors edit `docs-src/` and never touch these directly.
/README.md
/README.fr.md
/docs/ai-integration.md
/docs/ai-integration.fr.md
/docs/cli-reference.md
/docs/cli-reference.fr.md
/docs/mcp-reference.md
/docs/mcp-reference.fr.md

# Local design / planning docs that should never be committed. User-maintained
# scratchpads consumed by the AI agent across sessions ; tracked content
# would create noise on every doc iteration without serving repo consumers.
/UST_LUA_SPEC.md
/SOURCEMAP_v1.md
